  "racePreview": {
    "slug": "qatar-s-tyre-challenge-antonelli-s-crown-verstappen-s-charge-mwz6kwj1",
    "round": 22,
    "raceSlug": "qatar",
    "title": "Qatar GP",
    "season": "2026",
    "country": "Qatar",
    "flag": "qa",
    "raceStart": "2026-11-29T16:00:00.000Z",
    "publishedAt": "2026-11-27",
    "headline": "Qatar's Tyre Challenge: Antonelli's Crown, Verstappen's Charge",
    "summary": "The titles are sorted, but Qatar's brutal circuit means the fights for second and third in both championships are heating up. Expect tyre strategy to be key in the desert.",
    "body": "Kimi Antonelli and Mercedes have already bagged both championships, but don't think Qatar's a dead rubber—there’s still plenty to scrap for. Max Verstappen, fresh off a Las Vegas win and four victories in his last six, is pushing hard to lock down P2 in the drivers’ standings. He's got a decent gap on Lewis Hamilton, George Russell, and Lando Norris, but with two races left, nothing’s guaranteed. Ferrari's in a strong spot for second in the Constructors', but Red Bull and McLaren are practically breathing down each other's necks for third — just nine points in it. Plus, the drama from Vegas is still simmering, with Verstappen and Russell having a public spat, and another Hamilton-Leclerc clash leaving Fred Vasseur with a major headache.\n\nLusail is a proper tyre-killer, packed with 16 high-speed corners that just punish the rubber, especially that front-left. Pirelli’s slapped a strict 27-lap limit on each tyre set, forcing everyone into a minimum two-stop race — so strategy's going to be massive. There are hardly any slow corners here to give the tyres a breather, making it one of the most demanding circuits all year. Overtaking isn't exactly easy either, so nailing quali will be crucial. Verstappen loves this place, winning the last three Qatar GPs. With only Audi bringing a minor upgrade, most teams are just trying to survive these brutal conditions.",
    "picks": {
      "winner": "Verstappen",
      "wildcard": "Norris"
    }
  },
